&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Sony Interactive Entertainment?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sony Interactive Entertainment isn’t just the Best Place to Play — it’s also the Best Place to Work. Sony Interactive Entertainment (SIE) is the company behind the PlayStation brand. As a subsidiary of Sony Group Corporation, we’re part of a proud legacy of innovation and excellence. SIE is a dynamic technology company, delivering cutting-edge hardware and network services to more than 100 million people and an entertainment leader, home to some of the most beloved and recognizable intellectual properties (IP) in the world. Our role at SIE is to create and nurture the experiences under the PlayStation brand, a name synonymous with entertainment excellence and creativity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(31, 56, 100); font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job description&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;color: !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;The successful candidate will join the Security Data Analytics team, working across PlayStation data assets and business groups.&amp;nbsp;This team develops the data products, pipelines, dashboards, and reporting that help Information Security teams understand security posture, risk trends, control effectiveness, exposure, and remediation progress.&amp;nbsp; Our work is increasingly built on automation and AI-enabled analytics, and this role builds the data foundations that make that possible.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;color: !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;This opening focuses on the backend of that work.&amp;nbsp; Reporting to the Director of Security Data Analytics, you will design and operate the data engineering foundations our analytics depend on: ingestion and transformation pipelines, Snowflake data models, automation, and the enrichment and AI-ready data patterns that turn raw security signals into trusted, analytics-ready data.&amp;nbsp;Presentation-layer engineers own most visualization delivery, so your primary contribution is the reliability, structure, and performance of the data layer, including keeping it running day to day.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;color: !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;This is a technical, individual contributor role.&amp;nbsp; You will solve moderately complex problems with limited supervision and own a discrete workstream or a sub-set of a larger effort, working closely with a global set of stakeholders.&amp;nbsp; This role is UK-based and remote-eligible.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;color: !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(31, 56, 100); font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12

&lt;p&gt;Qube Research &amp;amp; Technologies (QRT) is a global quantitative and systematic investment manager, operating in all liquid asset classes across the world. We are a technology- and data-driven group implementing a scientific approach to investing. Combining data, research, technology, and trading expertise has shaped our collaborative mindset, which enables us to solve the most complex challenges. QRT’s culture of innovation continuously drives our ambition to deliver high-quality returns for our investors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will join the Infrastructure Database team responsible for managing and optimising large-scale database systems supporting research and trading activities. The team works closely with Quantitative Researchers, Developers, and Data Engineers to ensure reliability, scalability, and performance of critical data infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Future Role within QRT&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Administer and maintain ClickHouse clusters in distributed environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Configure and manage replication, sharding, and distributed table architectures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate and maintain ClickHouse Keeper or ZooKeeper&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage data lifecycle processes including partitioning, TTL, and merge operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor database performance and troubleshoot issues in high-throughput environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimise query performance through indexing strategies, partitioning, and projections&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage system resources including CPU, memory, and disk I/O for database workloads&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement high availability and disaster recovery solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support database environments across production and non-production setups&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement and maintain access control, roles, and security policies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with data ingestion pipelines including streaming and batch frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to database reliability, observability, and scalability improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Present Skillset&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in database administration in production environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience with ClickHouse in distributed or clustered setups&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of replication, sharding, and distributed database architectures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with ClickHouse Keeper or ZooKeeper&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of performance tuning, monitoring, and troubleshooting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting high-ingestion and large-scale analytical workloads&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in SQL and database design principles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with UNIX/Linux systems and system-level performance tuning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of high availability an

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Position&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an engineer with a strong background in mobile device management (MDM) and remote device solutions. You will play a key role in engineering, managing and maintaining a growing fleet of thousands of iOS and Android devices and ensuring seamless connectivity to essential apps and services that support our business needs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this position, you’ll focus on improving, automating and standardising our fleet of corporately owned and BYOD-managed mobile devices and its supporting infrastructure. This will involve developing and maintaining scripts, optimising MDM systems and collaborating globally to resolve issues, deploy updates and enhance systems in this growing and fast-moving domain. You will also develop new solutions for business problems and architect integrations to meet the requirements of a variety of stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong communication and interpersonal skills will be needed as you collaborate with colleagues across the firm globally to find and resolve issues, plan and execute deployments and improve systems where possible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Getting the details right and keeping good records are critical in this role. Good troubleshooting skills are essential and you’ll be expected to clearly document problem resolution resulting from root cause analysis.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is part of our IT Engineering group, a dedicated team that architects and manages a global physical, virtual and mobile computing environment. Your analytical skills and expertise will directly support our colleagues and ensure the highest standard of system performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive hands-on experience engineering MDM/UEM platforms at scale, managing iOS fleets across corporate-owned and BYOD models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience with automation and scripting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experienced with MDM platforms such as Intune, Jamf Pro or Workspace One&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in managing Apple device lifecycles using Apple Business Manager.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a demonstrated ability to integrate various systems to fulfil business needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent troubleshooter and communicator with a strong customer service mentality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A flexible and reliable team player who enjoys working in a collaborative environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing BYOD Android devices is beneficial but not required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in English required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
